<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine Jan-Nov GDP falls 10.1 pct year-on-year.</title>
<headline>Ukraine Jan-Nov GDP falls 10.1 pct year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukranian gross domestic product in the first 11 months of this year was 69.4 billion hrynia, 10.1 percent less than a year earlier, the Ministry of Statistics said on Friday.</p>
<p>    UKRAINE GDP		   Jan-Nov 96  Jan-Oct 96  Jan-Nov 95</p>
<p>    Year-on-year pct change     -10.1	 -10.0	 -12.0</p>
<p>The Ukranian government is forecasting GDP will probably fall 7-8 percent over the whole of the year, after falling 11.8 percent in 1995, and could rise about 1.5-1.8 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
